) (xy 373.38 220.98)) (stroke (width 0) (type default)) (uuid "6936bd68-8dca-4566-9b54-ebe20ff9d82f")) (label "GND" (at 373.38 220.98 180) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify right bottom)) (uuid "d7129f8a-4036-412c-9f84-a271dd8c1a47")) (wire (pts (xy 378.46 223.52) (xy 373.38 223.52)) (stroke (width 0) (type default)) (uuid "18fbc26a-32b0-44bb-b6f3-93de1d10d60a")) (label "+8V4_IN" (at 373.38 223.52 180) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify right bottom)) (uuid "6d328ff0-4b29-468a-b468-b64c2ffa7b33")) (wire (pts (xy 378.46 226.06) (xy 373.38 226.06)) (stroke (width 0) (type default)) (uuid "3ca952fd-4ece-419e-9a08-1468f52fd7d8")) (label "GND" (at 373.38 226.06 180) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify right bottom)) (uuid "4ac980c3-c097-41dc-ac76-25470c683561")) (text "HastaDAQ" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 20 0) (effects (font (size 3 3) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "1adcab29-e11b-4f68-83e4-56b0e2add27e")) (text "Net labels connect everything: same name = same net. +3V3 / GND are plain labels, not power symbols." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 27 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "e0315ca0-5e61-4bce-bec1-6818cadb00e4")) (text "Pimoroni Pico Plus 2 (+ RM2 on SP/CE): same 40-pin header as Pico 2 W. Qwiic port = GP4/GP5 (I2C0), same nets as\nheader pins 6/7 and 3V3 as pin 36. Each ADS122C04 board also has two Qwiic connectors in parallel with its\nVIN/GND/SDA/SCL pins. Crossed-out pins are intentionally unused." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 36 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "1a921df3-8413-4eb8-869e-19e0b452ad97")) (text "NOTES\n1. ONE common GND (Pico, sensors, servo PSU). SBUS needs a shared ground reference.\n   RM2 WiFi breakout: SP/CE uses GP32-GP36 only, no overlap with Qwiic (GP4/5) or any other signal.\n2. ADS2: bridge one address jumper on its back (A0/A1); resulting address unconfirmed --\n   firmware falls back to an I2C scan at boot.\n3. Each half-bridge module (2 gauges) plugs into a 3-pin header: V, SIG (mid-point), GND. The two fixed\n   350R completion resistors sit next to the ADC; their mid-point goes to A1. Excitation is the ADC's own\n   VIN, so VREF_SUPPLY is ratiometric -- no Ref+/Ref- wiring.\n4. SBUS: GP20 (TX) and GP21 (RX) on one net (UART inverted in firmware).\n5. POWER: 8.4 V bench PSU -> fuse -> VSERVO feeds the servos directly and the UBEC input. UBEC 5 V -> Schottky ->\n   Pico VSYS. Pico VSYS max is 5.5 V (datasheet), so the UBEC MUST be set to 5 V, not 6 V. Confirm the UBEC's\n   input range covers 8.4 V. USB (VBUS) is left for programming. Set a current limit on the bench PSU.\n6. Trigger pins are 3.3 V logic only. Pin order on the headers: see each symbol.\n   Power connector (8-wire): 1,8 GND | 2,7 V supply (8.4 V) | 3,6 sensor GND | 4 trigger OUT | 5 trigger IN.\n   Sensor GND (3,6) is drawn tied to the common GND; split it only if the sensor return must stay separate.\n7. Per ADC: 1k in each bridge-output leg + 100nF across them (~800 Hz corner), and 10uF + 100nF across the\n   bridge supply. Place these at the ADC end. Use shielded twisted cable for the gauge wires, shield to GND at\n   the ADC end only." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 110 281 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "a121873f-f1a1-4513-b63f-9646e881fd70")) (sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1"))) (embedded_fonts no))